From 34a3144fe09b3d5633f31b966d97ae8bf424f4ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:24:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a courier card restored from the Board
 publishes its exact origin marker again

origin_creation_intents is machine-local and its binding_id is a random secret, so a
gateway reprovisioned from the Board got its courier cards back without their intent
rows. The hermes-hub collector publishes a card's origin_bindings only from that table,
so it republished them as [] and the origin gateway's ledger
(kanban_origin_ledger._advanced_observation) never advanced the obligation again
(fail-closed, but the origin chat never saw completion; an in-flight receipt stayed
origin_publication_pending) (t_01a1cf7ee5a6103e).

create_with_origin / adopt_with_origin now append one synced task event,
origin_intent_recorded, holding the whole intent row, in the same transaction. When the
sync apply inserts that event for a card the file got back from the Board
(kanban_restored_cards, primary live file only) and the binding names this gateway and
this card as owner, the exact row is re-inserted (INSERT OR IGNORE, never changed).
Foreign copies, unmarked cards and malformed payloads are skipped. Local gc_events keeps
the kind like 'decomposed'. Residual gap: the Board service drops events after 30 days,
so a card open longer than that before it was lost still fails closed as before.

Measured first: 0 unreleased obligations in the hub ledgers (default 156 rows, bb-tuner
16) name a worker-N owner; 2 of 1093 worker-owned records in the hub replica ever carried
origin_bindings (worker-1 t_01a1cdcdd0627aaa, worker-2 t_01a1ce02b36b6969, both done,
macbook origin). The path is live but rare, so the fix is small and additive.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_restore_origin_intents.py. RED on the base:
after the restore the republished record has origin_bindings=[] and the obligation stays
at observation 1 (create and adopt), no carry event, gc drops it; the installed hermes-hub
collector publishes origin_bindings=[] after the restore. GREEN 4/4, and the installed
collector republishes the exact marker.
